   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 22.28,
   "text": "Kwame was not done. Power to the people, Abeg, with soldiers and curfews. The revolution promised exactly that. It set up people's and workers' defense committees in neighborhoods and workplaces, later renamed committees for the defense of the revolution, so ordinary Ghanaians could watch prices, expose corruption, and hold power to account.",
